   "result": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose is above the labeled maximum. Amlodipine is approved up to **10 mg once daily** for adults. Doses above that raise the risk of peripheral edema, hypotension, and reflex tachycardia without much added BP lowering. Your patient's normal renal and hepatic function and lack of allergies don't change that ceiling.\n\nHere are some options:\n\n1. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO once daily**, the max labeled dose.\n2. **Amlodipine 10 mg PO daily plus a second agent** such as an ACE inhibitor, ARB, or thiazide-like diuretic, if the goal is more BP control. Combining classes is usually more effective and better tolerated than pushing the dose.\n3. **Amlodipine 20 mg PO once daily as written**, if you intend an off-label dose. I'd need your explicit confirmation, and many pharmacy systems will require a documented indication or override reason.\n\nPlease tell me which you'd like. If you confirm 20 mg, include the clinical rationale for the override.\n\nI also don't have an order-entry tool connected in this session, so I can only prepare the order text for you to sign in your EHR once the dose is settled.",
